          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Anxiety sits in the mental and behavioural chapter. Where would a physical symptom of it, like palpitations, be classified?",
          "answer": "In the ICD-10 system, if palpitations are attributed to anxiety, both conditions would be classified.\n\nAnxiety is categorized within Chapter 5: Mental, behavioral and neurodevelopmental disorders, specifically in the range of F40 to F48 (coding-icd10-chapter-05-mental). This chapter includes phobias, panic, generalized anxiety disorder, and stress-related conditions.\n\nPalpitations, as a physical symptom, are classified in Chapter 18: Symptoms, signs, and abnormal findings. Codes R00 to R09 cover symptoms related to the circulatory and respiratory systems, and palpitations specifically fall into this range (coding-icd10-chapter-18-symptoms).\n\nWhen a symptom like palpitations is caused by an underlying condition such as anxiety, both codes are typically reported. The anxiety would be listed as the primary diagnosis, and the palpitations would be an additional code to describe the specific physical manifestation (coding-insomnia-g47, coding-icd10-chapter-18-symptoms).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
